tags: device-time

A rate of the node: the price of one device that is attached to an instance, for each
hour.

The value is MU for one device for one hour. Example: 5000000. The node charges in
proportion to the time, and rounds each charge down to a whole MU.

The scope selects the devices: the id of the formal of a model fact (for example
pci-model, 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:f77f111c3a3c9e36622b21845ab2e344fafb2b47f10ae9854b4d58649b751c28), then "=", then the value of that fact, as UTF-8.
Example: <id of pci-model>=10de:2330. An empty scope is the general rate. A reader that
does not know the rate ignores it.

=== formal
base=one device for 3600 seconds
class=rate
name=device-time
of=one device attached to an instance
rounding=the node computes each charge in proportion and rounds it down to a whole MU
scope=<id of the formal of a fact of the device>=<value of that fact>, as text of the concept 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:24801bc1176a41ff5f2aa2b94f8a3186eb42a69b5d68437e6e849c83bb443895; empty: the general rate
